WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.080
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.760
Back by popular demand,
it’s the NutritionFacts Grab Bag,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.800
where we look at the latest science
on a whole variety of topics.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.120
And we start with a story on the FDA-
approved bioidentical hormones

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.320
that skirt the standardization concerns
of compounded preparations.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.000
The news that
menopausal hormone therapy

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.960
had the potential to cause
higher rates of breast cancer,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.160
cardiovascular disease,
and overall harm

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.880
rocked women and physicians
across the country.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.720
The study arm used progesterone
and Premarin,

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.400
because it was the most commonly
prescribed form of estrogen

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.280
and is still prescribed

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.120
more than a million times
a year in the U.S.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.800
It's a mixture of more
than 50 different estrogens

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.640
from horse pee.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.000
("Premarin" comes from the words
"pregnant mare urine,"

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.840
if you're skeptical,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.440
try crushing a pill
and sniffing it.)

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.000
The dour findings
of the Women's Health Initiative

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.640
(combined with some high-profile
celebrity endorsements)

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.880
saw interest shift
to "bioidentical hormones,"

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.800
made from plants
rather than a horse source.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.800
They are marketed as being safer
and more effective.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.920
No wonder estimates
peg the annual number

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.680
of prescriptions
at 30 million a year,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.760
constituting
a billion-dollar industry.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.000
One reason patients may believe
compounded hormone therapy

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.480
is safer is that,
thanks to a legal loophole,

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.240
they are not mandated
to provide

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.080
the FDA insert required
for commercial products

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.080
warning about side effects.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.880
Purchased at regular pharmacies,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.080
hormones have
a prominent black box

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.240
with an all-caps
"WARNING: ENDOMETRIAL CANCER,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.040
CARDIOVASCULAR DISORDERS,
BREAST CANCER,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.320
AND PROBABLE DEMENTIA."

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.800
There's no evidence
that bioidentical hormones

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.840
are any safer,

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.080
but the missing laundry list
of side effects

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.000
may give patients
a false sense of security.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.640
Another appeal
is customized dosing

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.800
based on saliva hormone testing,

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.000
but such tests are considered
to be unreliable

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.240
and so recommended against,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.800
since the only people
who profit

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.400
are the ones
trying to sell you the tests.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.680
Custom-compounded hormones
are not FDA-approved,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.000
have not been shown to be safer
or more effective,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.520
and may lack standardization
of quality, purity, and dose.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.960
When the FDA
or muckraking journalists

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.440
have filled
the same prescriptions

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.960
in compounding pharmacies
in different states,

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.280
a third of the stated
estrogen contents

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.840
were off
by as much as 250 percent.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.880
No wonder all the major
American medical societies

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.440
that counsel physicians
on treating menopausal women

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.440
recommend against
compounded hormones,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.400
including the American College
of Obstetrics and Gynecology,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.480
the Endocrine Society,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.480
and the North American
Menopause Society.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.520
Characterizing the pushback
they got from their 2020 review

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.560
recommending against the use
of bioidentical hormones,

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.360
the National Academies
of Sciences,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.600
Engineering,
and Medicine concluded,

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.080
"It is clear
from these communications

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.120
that many clinicians,
compounding pharmacists,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.600
and patients hold minimum,
if any,

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.880
concerns regarding
the medication's safety

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.920
and effectiveness."

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.160
Now, as of 2019,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.840
there are pee-free FDA-approved
bioidentical hormones

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.160
that skirt
the standardization concerns

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.160
of compounded preparations,

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.040
but that just brings us back
to square one,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:28.840
since they are considered

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.360
to have
the same risk/benefit profile.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.520
The multibillion-dollar
compounded hormone industry

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.440
is considered a "leading source
of disinformation,"

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.120
but the same could be said
of Big Pharma.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.280
With so many billions of dollars
at stake,

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.400
it's hard to know
who to trust.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.480
When in doubt,
I turn to The Medical Letter

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.880
on Drugs and Therapeutics,

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.200
considered one
of the least biased sources

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.360
in medicine.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.160
It's kind of like
the Consumer Reports

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.480
of the drug world,
and, in fact,

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.480
was actually co-founded
by the co-founder

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.160
of the publisher
of Consumer Reports

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.560
more than 50 years ago.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.280
As The Medical Letter
used to brag on their website,

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.920
it "does not accept grants,
from any source;

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.000
donations, from anyone;
[or] funding, from any entity."

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.280
They won't let their work be
used for promotional purposes,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.720
and they don't accept
any advertising.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.960
In their review of the evidence,
they concluded,

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.480
"There is no acceptable evidence

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.520
that bio-identical hormones
are safer."

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.320
So, how do you treat
menopausal symptoms

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.600
like hot flashes?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.040
The American College of
Obstetricians and Gynecologists

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.160
suggests palliative measures,
such as "consuming cool drinks,"

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.760
but is there really no way
to treat hot flashes

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.920
without the cancer, clots,
and coronaries?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.680
Thankfully there is,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.920
as I cover in a video series
that starts with

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.840
Menopausal Hot Flashes
Are Not Inevitable

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.920
and then moves
from prevention to treatment.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.680
In our next story,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.920
we look at how laser
therapy is marketed

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.520
as a promising alternative
to drugs and scalpels

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.400
for treating hair loss.
But does it work?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.480
In my book, How Not to Age,

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.920
I discuss all the drugs,
foods, supplements,

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.280
and surgeries that can treat
age-related hair loss,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.480
but what about non-dietary,
non-drug,

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.800
non-surgical interventions?

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.520
Autologous platelet-rich plasma,

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.680
where concentrated portions
of your own blood

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.720
is repeatedly injected
into your scalp,

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.920
appears to have an efficacy
similar to the available drugs,

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.880
though the available evidence
is considered insufficient

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.360
to recommend it,
and so remains unapproved

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.800
in the U.S. or Europe
for hair restoration purposes.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.080
Scalp Botox
is also not recommended.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.560
The thought was
that relaxing scalp muscles

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.640
might improve blood flow,

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.000
but when actually put
to the test

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.480
actually caused hair loss

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.960
in some pilot study
participants.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.680
Then, there are lasers.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.760
In the 1960s,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.120
a Hungarian physician
published the paper,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.640
"The effect of laser beams
on the growth of hair in mice,"

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.560
detailing
a serendipitous discovery

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.880
that a low-powered ruby laser
increased the hair growth

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.360
on the shaved backs of mice.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.440
The mechanism appears to be
increased blood flow.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.880
The floodgates opened
when the FDA cleared

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.080
the first low-level
laser therapy device

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.400
for age-related
pattern hair loss in 2007,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.800
and now, there are clinics
advertising lasers

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.440
for everything
from tennis elbow

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.960
to "scrotal rejuvenation."

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.920
There have been at least ten
randomized, controlled trials

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.840
of low-level
laser therapy devices

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.040
for hair loss, and the efficacy
has been found comparable

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.360
or even superior to the drugs.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.320
They are noninvasive and appear
to be relatively safe.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.480
Mild side effects
include itching, acne,

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:43.720
and scalp tenderness

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.240
that usually resolves
within two weeks.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.760
Reviews typically conclude
that laser therapy

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.280
may be a promising alternative
to drugs and scalpels,

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.520
but there remains
considerable skepticism

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.800
within the dermatology community

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.640
and for good reason.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.480
Most of the laser therapy trials

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.440
were funded
by the manufacturers

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.840
of the tested products
themselves.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.200
This is true of hair loss
treatments across the board,

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:12.040
but laser studies appear
particularly reticent

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.440
to provide visual evidence
or inquire

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.960
about perhaps the most important
outcome of all,

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.880
patient satisfaction.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.200
When the first independent study
was performed,

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.920
blinded evaluations
of before-and-after photographs

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.720
could not detect a difference
in hair density or caliber.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.800
In two studies that compared
subjective satisfaction

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.640
between laser
and sham placebo devices,

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.120
no significant difference
could be found either.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.000
In other words,
from the patient's perspective,

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.200
they just plain don't work.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.280
So, while there are

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:46.920
statistically significant
improvements

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.680
in hair density and thickness,

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:52.840
there may be little clinically
significant improvement.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.000
If you want to give them
a try anyway,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.480
there are at least 29
FDA-cleared devices

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.000
currently on the market.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.160
There have been no head-to-head
studies between them,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.680
but based on measured outcomes,

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.600
there appear to be
no difference

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.040
between the comb-style
and hat-style devices,

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.680
though those containing
laser diodes exclusively

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:12.960
may have an edge over devices

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.200
that include a mix
of both laser diodes and LED.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.120
Do not look into the light,

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.400
as prolonged retinal exposure
could be damaging.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.840
Thankfully,
at least most cap designs

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.600
have a built-in safety shut-off

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.800
to avoid accidental
eye exposure.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.680
Otherwise,
besides general safety caveats

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.600
about using
electrical contraptions

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:34.800
in or around water,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.240
such devices are
considered safe,

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.160
though they are contraindicated

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.400
for those with cancer
of the scalp

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:45.520
due to the potential
for stimulatory effects.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.160
Finally today,

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.360
we hear about astralagus root,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.080
one of the most popular herbs
in traditional Chinese medicine

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.800
that is marketed as
a “life-prolonging” tonic.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.720
In 2008, it was reported
that a screening

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.720
of traditional
Chinese medicine plants

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.000
identified a compound
called cycloastragenol

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.400
in the roots
of the astragalus plant

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.560
that appeared
to moderately enhance

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.360
telomerase activation.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.120
That's an enzyme
I've covered before

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.160
that our body uses
to try to reverse one aspect

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.640
of cellular aging
by elongating your telomeres,

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.520
the protective caps
on your chromosomes.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:24.440
Three years later,

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.560
after it was shown
to elongate short telomeres

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.720
and improve healthspan
(though not lifespan) in mice,

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.520
a one-year human trial
was published.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.160
Although in most of the subjects

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.560
telomeres continued
to shorten on average,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.520
there did seem to be
a significant reduction

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:42.040
in the proportion of cells
with critically short telomeres.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.640
And the side effects
looked good,

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.280
including a drop
in LDL cholesterol

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.840
and blood pressure.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.480
But there was no control group

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.760
and cycloastragenol
(branded as "TA-65")

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.760
was but one
of over fifty vitamins,

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.880
minerals, herbs,
and other compounds they gave

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:59.480
to the research subjects
that year.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.200
When TA-65 was finally
properly put to the test

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.120
in randomized controlled trials,

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.720
there was no cholesterol

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.080
or blood pressure benefit
whatsoever,

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.640
but in cytomegalovirus-positive
patients,

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.800
a significant
telomere-lengthening effect

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.560
was demonstrated at one dose
but not another.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.160
(Those with
chronic viral infections,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.680
such as CMV or HIV,

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.480
tend to have white blood cells

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.480
with especially truncated
telomeres.)

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:28.040
The only such study
showing clinical benefit

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.600
was a year-long pilot study
of TA-65

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.840
for early age-related
macular degeneration,

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.880
though it was funded
by the company

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.440
that sells it
for $600 a bottle.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.080
They grossed
more than $50 million

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.960
before the Federal
Trade Commission charged them

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.360
with false and deceptive
claims and practices.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.160
That $600
buys you less than a gram

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.520
of astragalus root extract.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:54.960
You can buy
astragalus root extract in bulk

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:59.320
50,000 times cheaper
for less than $20 a pound,

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.880
should there ever be
independently verified benefits.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:06.560
Astragalus root,
well-known as huáng qí in China,

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.360
is one of the most popular herbs
in traditional Chinese medicine,

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.880
included in hundreds
of herbal formulas

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.400
and evidently widely marketed

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.840
for millennia
as a "life prolonging" tonic.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.280
No data on that,

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.480
but about 30 grams a day
appeared to help

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.000
with a type
of autoimmune kidney disease

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.200
called idiopathic
membranous nephropathy

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.800
in 50 randomized
controlled trials,

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.560
but not
placebo-controlled trials;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:33.920
so, any placebo effects
can't be discounted.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.200
Pregnant or nursing women

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.760
are cautioned against
using astragalus,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.920
and a theoretical concern
was raised

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.760
that it may activate
a certain oncogene,

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.080
a potentially
cancer-causing gene.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:45.880
However,
dozens of randomized trials

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.880
of astragalus-based
herbal preparations

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:50.480
as an add-on therapy
to chemotherapy

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.600
for the most common type
of lung cancer

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.760
(non-small-cell) found,
if anything,

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.320
astragalus to be protective.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:02.280
Lung cancer is the leading cause
of cancer death in the U.S.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.680
Adding astragalus
to standard platinum-based chemo

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:08.600
reduced the risk of death
as much as 38 percent

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.120
at the one-year-mark,
and 25 percent at two years.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.680
However, in almost all trials,

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:17.560
the astragalus was just one
of many herbs used in a formula,

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.120
making the effects of astragalus
impossible to tease out,

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:22.160
and unfortunately,

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.880
publication bias
is widespread

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.240
in the traditional
Chinese medicine literature,

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.800
where inconvenient results
may be quietly shelved,

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:34.160
though this in no way
unique to that field.

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.800
Similar remarkable results,
with similar critical caveats,

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.040
were published for
astragalus-containing formulas

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.800
for colorectal cancer,

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.560
including
improved quality of life.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.240
Same thing with cervical cancer,

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:49.040
with remarkably reduced
chemotherapy toxicity:

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.400
less nausea and vomiting,

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.960
less hair loss,

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.520
less nerve damage,

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:56.760
and less liver
and kidney toxicity.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.680
Also, less lung damage
from radiation treatments,

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.120
and for stomach cancer,

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:05.560
improved quality of life
and quantity of life.

